Fix Multilink PPP, which cannot form a bundle on pppd 2.5.x

OpenWrt's own 321-multilink_support_custom_iface_names.patch rewrote the
member-side bundle lookup in mp_join_bundle() to find the holder by interface
name instead of by unit number, and made a new database field mandatory:

	if (!parse_num(rec.dptr, "PPPD_PID=", &pppd_pid)
	    || !parse_str(rec.dptr, "IFNAME=", tmp, sizeof(tmp))
	    || !parse_num(rec.dptr, "IFUNIT=", &unit)
	    || !process_exists(pppd_pid)
	    || !owns_link(pid, tmp))
		unit = -1;

The same patch added the only writer of IFUNIT=, guarded by "#ifdef USE_TDB".
That macro was renamed to PPP_WITH_TDB in pppd 2.5.0 and occurs nowhere in the
2.5.x tree, so setenv_ifunit() compiles to an empty function while the reader
above still requires what it would have written.

Every member link therefore leaves the lookup with unit == -1, never reaches
bundle_attach(), and falls through to make_new_bundle() -- which tries to create
an interface that the bundle holder already owns:

	pppd[4830]: CHAP authentication succeeded
	pppd[4830]: Couldn't create ppp interface hy-hyena: File exists
	pppd[4830]: Exit.

The failure arrives one line after a successful authentication and names the
interface, so it reads as a naming or authentication problem. It is neither: the
bundle key, the holder's pid and its UNIT= record are all correct and all agree.
Multilink PPP simply cannot form a bundle on any OpenWrt carrying pppd >= 2.5.0.

The patch dates from the 2.4.x era and still applies cleanly, which is why it
went silent rather than failing to build.

Signed-off-by: luunarrr <crystalguo42@gmail.com>

--- a/pppd/sys-linux.c
+++ b/pppd/sys-linux.c
@@ -1114,7 +1114,7 @@ void cfg_bundle(int mrru, int mtru, int
 static void
 setenv_ifunit(void)
 {
-#ifdef USE_TDB
+#ifdef PPP_WITH_TDB
 	char tmp[11];
 	slprintf(tmp, sizeof(tmp), "%d", ifunit);
 	ppp_script_setenv("IFUNIT", tmp, 0);
